.TH CHTTPCLI_SET_ENGINE_NUM_REACTOR_THREADS 3 "2026-07-17" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads \- set the OS thread count of the async engine reactor of chttpclient
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads(size_t num_threads);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function configures how many OS threads the shared
ccol_event_loop reactor of the async engine, which serves Tier 2 and
Tier 3, gives to its poll and its dispatch. The rules for the
num_reactor_threads parameter of ccol_event_loop_create_with_mprocs
apply here too (see cthreadcomm.h): a value of 1 means one thread that
both polls and dispatches inline, and a larger value means one
dedicated poller thread and (num_threads - 1) dispatch worker threads.

By default the reactor sizes itself to sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN),
and falls back to 1 if that query fails. You get that default if you
never call this function, and also if you call it with
num_threads == 0. A positive num_threads overrides that automatic size
and pins the reactor to exactly that number of threads; a num_threads
of 0 puts the automatic size back. This function configures only the
construction of the shared reactor, independently of the settings of
any one chttpcli instance.

You can call this function only at two times: before the reactor ever
starts in this process (that is, before the first call to
chttpclient_do_async or to chttpclient_do_async_streaming anywhere),
or after the engine stops completely, which happens after every async
user of a chttpcli drops its reference and the automatic teardown
finishes. The reactor of chttpsvr_set_engine_num_reactor_threads
usually lives for the whole process, but this engine starts and stops
on its own with the Tier 2 and Tier 3 traffic, so the window for this
call comes back again and again instead of being one chance at the
start of the process.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success, if the call succeeds.
ccol_not_permitted, while the engine runs. Wait for the engine to stop
    completely first.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs (3),
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_logger (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_pooled (3),
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_num_reactor_threads (3)
